      "message": "Thanks for pulling this refactor out. Now I see what is making me feel weird.\n\nThis `while (written)` is bad because it\u0027ll make a process(btadapterd) busy loop until another process(CRAS) feeds data. (be aware that data I/O is asynchronous!)\n\nIf you experiment by adding a debug log here, I guess it\u0027s easy to see the busy loop - especially when SCO socket is up, but CRAS hasn\u0027t yet started stream I/O.\nBoth NB and WB applies. \n\nIMO the previous logic is more appropriate. When partial or non data comes from audio server, calculate and send some equivalent silence to SCO.",
